[Music]  what's 71 percent of the Earth's surface  being covered in water it's no surprise  there are hidden gems located beneath  the surface from buried treasures UFOs  and entire cities you never know what  you'll find when you take a dive if  you're new to our channel don't forget  to subscribe and please give this video  a big thumbs up because today we'll be  sharing 10 most amazing things ever  found underwater just wait until you see  the photos of a sunken pirate city in  the Caribbean we promise it'll shock you  the lost Egyptian city in the year 2000  French archaeologists discovered an  entire Egyptian city 30 feet below the  Mediterranean Sea known as her a Klien  the city was a vibrant and bustling town  judging by the artifacts that were found  numerous statues of ancient Pharaoh's  pieces of artwork coins made of gold  lead and bronze and a fleet of ships  were discovered on the floor of the sea  it's unknown how the city managed to get  submerged beneath the water many believe  the rising of the sea could have  swallowed the entire city or the town  was possibly the victim of a natural  disaster such as a tidal wave or a  massive earthquake a hidden River  scientists have discovered a river that  follows along the bottom of the Black  Sea deep-sea divers explored the area  and found that the river has its own  waterfalls trees and leaves the river's  layers of dense water were formed when  sinkholes became filled with saltwater  the water moves along the ocean floor at  a rate of a half a mile per day it's  like a whole new world below the surface  of the sea if this river were on land it  would be the sixth largest river in the  world would you like to take a deep-sea  adventure to visit this river let us  know in the comments section down below  the Pyramid of Yonaguni a scuba  instructor dived off the coast of the  Japanese island Yonaguni in 1996 and  what he discovered was shocking hidden  below the surface was a perfectly  designed pyramid complete with steps  columns and a human face carved inside  the rocks in the following years experts  visited the underwater site and  concluded it had been man made in  approximately 10,000 BC it's been said  that the pyramid sunk into the ocean  after a massive earthquake the Lion City  in 1959 the ancient Chinese city known  as Lion City was flooded on purpose to  make room for an  hydroelectric power station but then the  government forgot about the city for  years  it wasn't until 2001 when the government  decided to rediscover the city through  diving expeditions Lion City dates back  to 621 AD and even after being submerged  below water for years it's still in  pristine condition divers discovered  that many of the structures carvings and  lion statues were still preserved and  the water had protected it from natural  erosion deep in the Baltic Sea  Swedish divers uncovered a bizarre  discovery on the floor of the pelvic  scene measuring 60 metres in diameter  and standing on tall pillars divers  believed it may have been a UFO the  diving team also noticed a staircase  with a hole leading into the interior of  the object and they also claimed their  electrical equipment stopped working as  soon as they swam closer to the object  we may never know if it's an actual  alien spacecraft but we wouldn't be  surprised if it was do you think it's  possible a UFO crashed into the Baltic  Sea and sunk down deep into the water  let us know what you think down below  sunken pirate City at Port Royal the  city of Port Royal Jamaica was inhabited  by unruly pirates up until 1692 a huge  earthquake and tsunami shook the wet and  Sandy foundation of the town and sunk it  into the Caribbean excavations have  recovered historical documents preserved  food and various buildings the city had  plans to turn the sunken city into a  tourist destination but for now it has  practically been abandoned would you  travel to Jamaica to see this pirate  city the Titanic this legendary ship  sank in the North Atlantic Ocean on the  morning of April 15 1912 after colliding  with an iceberg during its maiden voyage  the RMS Titanic sank to the bottom of  the ocean the wreckage wasn't found  until 1985 when the ship was discovered  12,000 400 feet below the surface of the  water over time the ship's roof have  caved in and the decks have weakened but  it's still amazing to see photos of this  legendary ship that's a part of world  history underwater circles a scuba diver  stumbled upon a pretty interesting site  off the coast of Japan these geometric  sand patterns were found 80 feet below  sea level and they're six feet in  diameter known as the mystery circle  many people believe the pattern was  created by a UFO but it was later can  firm that it was actually the work of  Japanese puffer fish the fish create the  pattern during their mating ritual as a  way to protect their eggs pretty  interesting don't you think  a whale washes ashore there's no telling  what will wash ashore on any given day  due to natural causes or after being hit  by a boat propeller massive whales have  made their way on shore beachgoers are  usually perplexed and a little afraid to  see these thirteen thousand pound  creatures so close to land some whales  and sharks will even beach themselves  mass strandings of marine mammals date  back to the days of Aristotle have you  ever seen a beached animal leave your  reply down below in the comment section  and you might even get a reply from us  underwater sculpture park the world's  first underwater sculpture park was  created in the Caribbean Sea just west  of Grenada designed by British sculptor  Jason de Kerr Taylor the submerged  museum is open for public viewing  sculptures include statues of people  from the local community including a  circle of children holding hands a man  working at his desk with the typewriter  and a life-size man riding a bicycle  would you like to visit this Caribbean  attraction one day which of these  underwater findings did you love the  most  leave us a comment and the most original  reply will get pinned to our channel if  you'd like to see more videos like this  one don't forget to subscribe and hit  the thumbs up button thanks for watching  [Music]

